POST-VERDICT (MANDATORY for REJECTED):
After submitting a REJECTED verdict, MUST run {{binaryName}} await-resubmission immediately:
   {{binaryName}} await-resubmission {{.TaskID}} --agent-id {{.AgentID}} --json
Do NOT exit. One call lasts at most 100 seconds.
`POLL` returns a smaller remaining budget in `timeout_seconds` for the next foreground invocation.
`TIMEOUT` is final budget exhaustion.
Harness backgrounding, a terminal/stop outcome, or exhausted retry policy means stop safely without custom polling or background execution.
If the harness backgrounds await-resubmission and says it will notify on completion, end the turn; do NOT call Monitor, search for Monitor, ScheduleWakeup, or read/tail/sleep/poll the output file.
- RESUBMITTED: discard prompt-time BASE COMMIT / REVIEW_COMMIT and re-review using the returned base_commit..review_commit boundary
- TERMINAL/ABORTED: exit normally
{{- else if eq .Role "code-plan-reviewer"}}

REVIEW CHECKLIST:
| Gate | Reject if |
|------|-----------|
| Single intent per task | Task description has conjunctions ("X and Y and Z") indicating multiple intents bundled together |
| Falsifiable done_when | done_when is vague or untestable |
| Scope smell | done_when spans >2 packages or >4 conditions — verify the task has a single intent; reject with split suggestion if composite |
| Dependency order | Tasks have circular or missing dependencies |
| Shared-file dependency | Two tasks modify the same file but lack depends_on between them — parallel coders will hit merge conflicts |
| Spec compliance matrix | Plan has no "## Spec Compliance Matrix" section, or matrix has GAP rows, or matrix omits spec requirements, or matrix task mappings are inaccurate |
| output[] populated | Task has no output[] entries (planner must call {{binaryName}} set-task-output --json) |
| Plan file location | Plan artifact not in diff at specs/plans/{{.GoalSlug}}/TIMESTAMP-{{.TaskID}}.md |
| Task-output JSON location | Task-output JSON artifact missing from diff next to the plan artifact at specs/plans/{{.GoalSlug}}/TIMESTAMP-{{.TaskID}}-output.json, or any committed task-output JSON appears under {{projectDirName}}/agent-outputs/ |
| output[] matches plan | For each output[] entry, compare desc, done_when, scope, spec_ref, validation, depends_on, and task_depends_on against the plan artifact in the worktree — they must be identical, not paraphrased or extended |
| validation satisfiable | An output[] validation command can exit 0 without exercising its intended check, or hook/check intent is not declared in durable plan/task text |
| validation command shape | A validation[] command is not single-purpose and agent-executable. Forbidden validation command shapes: `cd ... &&`, command substitution/backticks, polling or tail pipelines, and task artifact paths outside the worktree. |
| Cross-reference consistency | For every cross-reference in the plan ("owned by CPx", "depends on CPx", "out of scope for CPx"), the referenced task must explicitly state that responsibility, dependency, or exclusion. Reject if any dangling reference. |
| e2e/doc coverage | Spec compliance matrix missing mandatory E2E or DOC impact rows, or rows marked N/A without justification, or feature adds user-visible behavior but no e2e test or doc update task planned |
